From: Oseni Ibrahim <oseniibrahim845@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 08:56:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Slave: resolve master symbols on the follower broker (symbol
 mapping)

The slave used the master's symbol name as-is. When the follower broker
uses a different name (EURUSD.m, EURUSDpro, GOLD for XAUUSD, DJ30 for
US30) every order for that symbol failed and SL/TP were normalized with
the wrong digits.

UpdateSlavePositionOrders() now passes the master symbol through
ResolveSlaveSymbol(), which tries in order:
  1. explicit mapping (InputSymbolMapping, ex: XAUUSD=GOLD;US30=DJ30)
  2. InputSymbolPrefix + symbol + InputSymbolSuffix
  3. the exact master name
  4. auto detect: a tradeable symbol with the same base name
     (EURUSD -> EURUSD.m / EURUSDpro), when InputSymbolAutoDetect=true

Results are cached per master symbol, the resolved symbol is added to
Market Watch, and every non-identity mapping is logged once. When no
symbol is found the master name is kept (previous behavior), a clear
message is logged, and resolution is retried after 60 seconds.

With default inputs, a symbol that exists on the follower broker
resolves to itself, so existing setups are unchanged.

